<title>USA: S&amp;P revises MidCap, SmallCap stock indexes.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P revises MidCap, SmallCap stock indexes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's on Tuesday announced revisions to its S&amp;P MidCap 400 and S&amp;P SmallCap 600 indexes.</p>
<p>Pioneer Natural Resources Co will be added to the S&amp;P MidCap 400 after the close of trading on August 8, Standard &amp; Poor's said in a statement. Pioneer will be formed by the merger of MidCap component Parker &amp; Parsley Petroleum Co and MESA Inc.</p>
<p>MESA will be replaced in the SmallCap 600 Index by Innovex Inc.</p>
<p>Tracor Inc will replace RDM Sports Group Inc in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 on August 8 because RDM has consistently traded at less than $1.00 a share.</p>
<p>After the close of trading on August 11, Central Parking Corp will replace Control Data Systems Inc in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600.</p>
<p>Control Data Systems is being acquired by the investment firm of Welsh, Carson, Anderson &amp; Stowe in a cash tender offer scheduled to expire at that time.</p>
</text>
